.TH TAMIL\-KEYBOARD\-SETUP 1 "August 2026" "tamil\-keyboard 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tamil\-keyboard\-setup \- enable a Tamil input method in the current session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tamil\-keyboard\-setup
.I layout
.br
.B tamil\-keyboard\-setup \-\-remove
.I layout
.br
.B tamil\-keyboard\-setup \-\-list
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tamil\-keyboard\-setup
adds a Tamil input method to the input sources of the desktop session it is
run from. The layouts themselves are provided by
.BR ibus\-m17n ;
this command only selects one.
.PP
It must be run as your own user, not through
.BR sudo ,
because it configures the session it inherits. That is also why it works on
Wayland as well as X11.
.PP
The requested layout is appended to your existing input sources. Nothing is
removed or replaced, and running the command twice is harmless.
.SH APPLYING THE CHANGE
If IBus is already running, the layout appears in your input source
switcher immediately and no restart is needed.
.PP
If IBus is not running yet \- which is the usual case right after
installing this package, since it pulls IBus in for the first time \- you
must
.B log out and log back in
before the layout will work. The session needs restarting for
applications to pick up IBus as their input method framework at all.
.PP
.B tamil\-keyboard\-setup
detects which situation you are in and tells you which applies.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-remove " layout"
Remove the layout from your input sources.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Print the current input sources.
.TP
.B \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary.
.SH LAYOUTS
.TP
.B tamil99
Tamil 99 keyboard, corresponding to the m17n:ta:tamil99 input method.
.TP
.B phonetic
Tamil Phonetic keyboard, corresponding to the m17n:ta:phonetic input method.
.SH EXAMPLES
Add the Tamil 99 layout:
.PP
.RS
.B tamil\-keyboard\-setup tamil99
.RE
.PP
Switch between input sources with Super+Space.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success and 1 if the layout name is unknown, the command is run
as root, or the desktop does not use GNOME input sources.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ibus\-setup (1),
.BR gsettings (1)
